### Separation of Responsibilities

| Responsibility | Layer | Classes | What it does NOT do |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Validation** | Service | [AuthenticationService](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/service/AuthenticationService.java) — `validateRegistration()` | No SQL, no UI dialogs |
| **Validation** | UI (local) | [ResumeBuilder](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/ResumeBuilder.java) — `validateInput()`, `isValidEmail()`, `isValidPhone()` | No business logic, no DB |
| **Rendering** | Resume | [ClassicTemplate](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/resume/ClassicTemplate.java), [ModernTemplate](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/resume/ModernTemplate.java), [MinimalTemplate](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/resume/MinimalTemplate.java) | No DB, no UI |
| **Persistence** | DAO | [UserDAO](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/dao/UserDAO.java), [LoginDAO](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/dao/LoginDAO.java) | No validation, no rendering |
| **Display** | UI | [LoginFrame](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/LoginFrame.java), [RegisterFrame](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/RegisterFrame.java), [Dashboard](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/Dashboard.java), [ResumeBuilder](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/ResumeBuilder.java) | No SQL, no hashing |

> [!TIP]
> **Why validation lives in the service layer, not the UI:** If validation were in `RegisterFrame`, a CLI version, REST endpoint, or unit test would have **zero validation**. By placing it in [AuthenticationService](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/service/AuthenticationService.java), every caller gets the same rules automatically.

