# Bullet 3 — Validation Components, Dynamic Template Rendering & PDF Generation

> *"Built modular, reusable validation components and dynamic template rendering across 3 resume formats with automated PDF generation."*

## 3.1 Modular, Reusable Validation Components

### Service-Layer Validation (Reusable Across Any Caller)

[AuthenticationService.java](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/service/AuthenticationService.java) — `validateRegistration()`:

| Check | Rule | Exception Message |
|---|---|---|
| Username | Cannot be null or empty (after trim) | `"Username cannot be empty!"` |
| Email | Cannot be null or empty (after trim) | `"Email cannot be empty!"` |
| Password | Cannot be null or empty | `"Password cannot be empty!"` |
| Confirm Password | Must equal password (`.equals()`) | `"Passwords do not match!"` |

Throws `IllegalArgumentException` with the exact user-facing message. The UI simply catches and displays — **zero duplication of validation logic**.

### UI-Layer Validation (Form-Specific)

[ResumeBuilder.java](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/ResumeBuilder.java) — `validateInput()`:

| Check | Method | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| Name | inline | Cannot be empty |
| Email | `isValidEmail()` | Regex: `^[A-Za-z0-9+_.-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+$` |
| Phone | `isValidPhone()` | Regex: `\\d{10,15}` (digits only, 10–15 chars) |
| Skills | inline | At least one skill required |
| Experience | inline | Cannot be empty **if** "Experienced?" is checked |

Both validation layers are **reusable** — the same `validateInput()` guards both the "Generate Resume" and "Save to Database" actions.

